A||||10||burdell1||Loses Power after it Rains||||||
Z||000000||burdell1||09-05-99||09:53 AM||||Whenever it has been raining or if I have had my car washed, it hesitates and wants to stall.  After it has been running for a little while (and I step on the gas alot) it starts running normal. Anybody have a similar problem?<br>
Z||000001||theogre||09-05-99||12:28 PM||||replace the plug wires, cap, and rotor. The TPS could also be flaky, but in your case, unless you are spraying the motor directly, I'd do the wires cap and rotor first.
Z||000002||SloPonti||09-05-99||02:08 PM||||check your air filter!!  after a good rain or when i wash my car water will go in the scoop part in front of the drivers side rear wheel and the water will force its way up to the air filter!  the engine is not able to breath and causes it to stall until it dries out!  this has happened to me several times! hope this fixes your problem
Z||000003||burdell1||03-28-2000||12:12 PM||||Any other ideas?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Oreif||03-28-2000||12:21 PM||||I had the same problem when I first bought my car. To verify if it's wires and cap, Just get a spray bottle fill it with water and start the car. spray a mist over the spark plug wires. If it stumbles replace wires. (If you do it at night you will actually see the arcing and corona of electicity around the wires!) ||||reg||1
Z||000005||deceler8||03-28-2000||12:30 PM||||At the very least, check inside the dist. cap...bet it's full of water. And it doesn't take much to cause the problem you describe.<P>If it's wet, the rotor will probably be corroded too.<P>Ash tray doors in the mail.||||reg||1
Z||000006||whamel||03-28-2000||12:50 PM||||I had a similar problem with my '88 2M4 - turns out it was the battery cable.  The cable is very long and is very hard to check visually.  Mine had a short in it and eventually one rainy day it engaged the starter and ran the car into a tree.||||reg||1
Z||000007||overlord||03-28-2000||07:35 PM||||i have a similar prob with my 84 2m4.<P>except it only does that in the winter when there is fluffy snow on the road..then it freezes up...arrhh..<P>through rain...runs sweet..go figure...and to test it i made sure i hit every puddle on the highway...didnt even want to hesistate aftewards...its just that damned snow..||||reg||1
Z||000008||Phil||03-28-2000||07:52 PM||||Real Flakey||||reg||1
Z||000009||daved||03-30-2000||12:34 AM||||Mine used to do that after a visit to the car wash. Recently had the oxygen sensor fail; after changing it, the problem disappeared.  I guess the moisture was shorting it out.  Worth giving it a shot of that spray!<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000010||theogre||03-30-2000||07:26 PM||||Use one of the Bosch O2 sensors. They are about the best built there is. As good or better than AC/Delco. I've lost count of how many times I've dunked mine by opening the decklid after it's rained.||||reg||1
